## Tests

**`apps/web/src/duos/DuosBoard.test.tsx`**: add a new `describe("R2092000 Play again on the result panel")` after the #1755 block, and import `type DuosPlayAgain` from `./context.ts`. Inside the describe, define:
- `const OVER: DuosView = { ...duosView(), result: CONCEDED };`
- `const HERE = { youOffered: false, teammateOffered: false, teammateHere: true, matchId: null };`
- `again(over: Partial<DuosPlayAgain> = {})`, which returns `{ status: HERE, offering: false, refusal: null, offer: vi.fn<() => void>(), ...over }`.

The tests:
- `"R2092000 the panel draws Play again beside Watch the replay when the route hangs it, and Back to Play together is no longer primary"`:
  - The chrome is `{ onWatchReplay: vi.fn(), onLeave: vi.fn(), playAgain: again() }`.
  - The button testids, in order, are `["duos-result-board", "duos-result-replay", "duos-result-again", "duos-result-back"]`.
  - The again button has `button-primary` and the text "Play again"; the back button lacks `button-primary`.
  - `duos-result-board` has focus, and a click on the again button calls `offer` once.
- `"R2092000 while the offer is in flight Play again is disabled and busy"`: with `offering: true`, the button is disabled and has `aria-busy="true"`.
- `"R2092000 no Play again before the server's read, and none once the teammate has left"`:
  - With `status: null`, there is no button and no status line.
  - After `cleanup()`, with `teammateHere: false`, there is no button and the status line reads "Your teammate has left" (`role="status"`).
- `"R2092000 no Play again in the co-op replay, nor without one, as on /dev/duos"`:
  - `{ replay: true, view: OVER }` with chrome `{ playAgain: again() }` shows neither id.
  - After `cleanup()`, `{ view: OVER }` with only `onLeave` shows `duos-result` without either id.

**`apps/web/src/duos/DuosRoute.test.tsx`**: add a new `describe("R2092000 Play again on the co-op result")` at the end.
- Imports: add `refusal`, `at`, `type Call` and `type Reply` to the stubServer import. Also import:
  - `PLAY_LEAN_SET_KEY` from `../game/playLean.ts`
  - `SERIES_POLL_SECONDS` from `@jackioh/server-config`
  - `MS_PER_SECOND` from `../game/clockConstants.ts`
  - `type DuosAgainStatus` from `../net/duos.ts`
- Constants: `AGAIN = "/api/duos/matches/dm-1/again"`, `FINISHED = duosView(3, { outcome: "win", winner: "b", reason: "concede" })`, and `HERE: DuosAgainStatus` with the same value as above.
- `serve(status: () => DuosAgainStatus, offer: (call: Call) => Reply = () => ({ status: 200, body: { matchId: null } }))` returns `stubServer(...)`. It answers the catalog (as the file's `beforeEach` does), `GET AGAIN` with `status()` and `POST AGAIN` with `offer(call)`.
- `finished()` renders `<DuosRoute matchId="dm-1" token="tok-duos" />` and opens `latest()` as the #1792 block's `open()` does. It then pushes `{ type: "view", view: FINISHED, legal: [] }` and returns the render result.
- `flush()`: `await act(async () => { await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 0)); });`
- Hooks: `beforeEach(() => { at("/duos/dm-1"); })` and `afterEach(() => { vi.useRealTimers(); at("/"); })`.

Each test first calls `serve`, then `finished()`, then `await flush()`. Below, "GET answers `k: v`" means the status function is `() => ({ ...HERE, k: v })`.

- `"R2092000 a live game's result offers Play again, a press sends one offer with the device's lean pick, and the status waits for the teammate"`:
  - Set `PLAY_LEAN_SET_KEY` to `"Classic"`.
  - Use `let offered = false`. GET answers `youOffered: offered`, and the POST handler sets `offered = true`.
  - Click the again button. Before any flush, it is disabled with `aria-busy="true"`.
  - After `flush()`:
    - There is one POST, with body `{ leanSet: "Classic" }`.
    - The status line reads "Waiting for your teammate…" (`role="status"`).
    - The button is enabled.
- `"R2092000 with the teammate's offer read, the panel says the teammate wants to play again, and a press makes the offer"`:
  - GET answers `teammateOffered: true`.
  - The status line reads "Your teammate wants to play again", and the button reads "Play again".
  - A click and a flush make one POST with body `{}`.
- `"R2092000 an offer answered with the new match takes the board to /duos/<id>, whose socket is the new match's, not the old one's"`:
  - GET answers `teammateOffered: true`, and POST answers `{ matchId: "dm-2" }`.
  - After a click and a flush, the pathname is `/duos/dm-2`.
  - Run `const old = latest(); route.rerender(<DuosRoute matchId="dm-2" token="tok-duos" />);`.
  - Then check:
    - `latest()` is not `old`, and its `url` contains `matchId=dm-2`.
    - `old.readyState` is 3.
    - `duos-result` is gone and `duos-connecting` shows.
- `"R2092000 a status read naming the new match takes the board there too"`:
  - GET answers `{ ...HERE, youOffered: true, teammateOffered: true, matchId: "dm-3" }`.
  - The pathname is `/duos/dm-3`, and no POST was made.
- `"R2092000 a teammate who has left hides Play again and is named in the status"`:
  - GET answers `teammateHere: false`.
  - There is no button, and the status line reads "Your teammate has left".
- `"R2092000 a refused offer shows the server's words"`:
  - POST answers `refusal(409, "update_required", "The cards changed since this game. Start a new one.")`.
  - After a click and a flush:
    - The status line holds that text, with `role="alert"`.
    - The button is enabled.
    - The pathname is still `/duos/dm-1`.
- `"R2092000 folding the result to Result and opening it again keeps the waiting status"`:
  - Use the same server as the first test, then click the again button and flush.
  - Click `duos-result-board`; `duos-result` is gone.
  - Click `duos-result-reopen`. With no flush, the status line reads "Waiting for your teammate…" and there is still only one POST.
- `"R2092000 the status is read again every SERIES_POLL_SECONDS while the result is up"`:
  - First call `vi.useFakeTimers({ toFake: ["setInterval", "clearInterval"] })`, as CoopPanel.test.tsx does.
  - Use `let wants = false`; GET answers `teammateOffered: wants`. There is one GET and no status line.
  - Set `wants = true`, then run `await act(async () => { await vi.advanceTimersByTimeAsync(SERIES_POLL_SECONDS * MS_PER_SECOND + 1); }); await flush();`.
  - There are now two GETs, and the status line says the teammate wants to play again.

